HST Office: Writer's OLE cache leaves another program's objects alone

When an object starts running (a formula inserted or opened), Writer's OLE cache unloads the least
recently used running objects beyond Office.Common/Cache/Writer/OLE_Objects (20). For an object
of another program on Windows (a MathType equation), unloading makes that program's OLE server
load the object. In a document with many MathType equations, inserting or opening a formula
evicted them one after another until MathType stopped in its endless "Too many windows are
open" box and the office had to be ended in Task Manager (tdf#45892, tdf#94334). Measured on
Windows with MathType 7.12: the box came with the default cache size and did not come with the
cache raised to 500 or with the equations not running.

The cache now unloads only the office's own objects (SotExchange::IsInternal); other objects stay
as they are. Unloading them freed little: their program runs outside the office.
Test: CppunitTest_sw_uibase_uiview, testOleCacheKeepsMathTypeObjects.

